				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$\frac{{\rm{I}}}{{{\rm{I}}}_{\max }}=1-{{\rm{e}}}^{-{\rm{t}}/{\rm{\tau }}},$$\end{document}IImax=1−e−t/τ, where t is the time between the P1 and P2 test pulses. Data are represented as mean ± SEM; n, the number of experiments are shown between parentheses. Asterisks indicate statistically significant differences in the presence of A1329D relative to WT (*P < 0.05). The parameters of the fits and the results of the statistical evaluation are displayed in Supplementary Table 1.
